###  Case clause fall-throughs
TypeScript can reports errors for fall-through cases in switch statement where the case clause is non-empty. This check is turned _off_ by default, and can be enabled using [`noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`](https://www.typescriptlang.org/tsconfig#noFallthroughCasesInSwitch).
#####  Example
With [`noFallthroughCasesInSwitch`](https://www.typescriptlang.org/tsconfig#noFallthroughCasesInSwitch), this example will trigger an error:
```

ts

switch (x % 2) {




case0: // Error: Fallthrough case in switch.




console.log("even");




case1:




console.log("odd");




break;




```

However, in the following example, no error will be reported because the fall-through case is empty:
```

ts

switch (x % 3) {




case0:




case1:




console.log("Acceptable");




break;




case2:




console.log("This is *two much*!");




break;




```

