TypeScript 2.0 adds a new [`skipLibCheck`](https://www.typescriptlang.org/tsconfig#skipLibCheck) compiler option that causes type checking of declaration files (files with extension `.d.ts`) to be skipped. When a program includes large declaration files, the compiler spends a lot of time type checking declarations that are already known to not contain errors, and compile times may be significantly shortened by skipping declaration file type checks.
