1: string;




```

Note that this does not imply tuples represent immutable arrays, but it is an implied convention.
##  Improved type inference for object literals
TypeScript 2.7 improves type inference for multiple object literals occurring in the same context. When multiple object literal types contribute to a union type, we now _normalize_ the object literal types such that all properties are present in each constituent of the union type.
Consider:
```

ts

