TypeScript 5.6 introduces a new intrinsic type called `BuiltinIteratorReturn` and a new `--strict`-mode flag called `--strictBuiltinIteratorReturn`. Whenever `IteratorObject`s are used in places like `lib.d.ts`, they are always written with `BuiltinIteratorReturn` type for `TReturn` (though you’ll see the more-specific `MapIterator`, `ArrayIterator`, `SetIterator` more often).
